course: dictionary
lesson: 7602
title: A land ruled by a prince
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A principality is a country or area ruled by a prince or princess. You can spot the clue inside the word: it comes from «prince». The sentence «Moscow was a small principality, a land ruled by a prince» explains it for you.
explain: Be careful, because the word can mean different things. «The Principality» with a capital P is often a name for Wales in the UK. In the Bible, «principalities» means spiritual powers, not countries at all. Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits.
explain: Context clues help here. Words like «tribute», «overlord» and «Mongols» show that a principality can be a smaller land under the power of a bigger one. When you are not sure, swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense.
fact: A principality is a country or area ruled by a prince or princess.
fact: Monaco and Liechtenstein are small principalities in Europe.
fact: «The Principality» with a capital P is sometimes used to mean Wales.
fact: In the Bible, «principalities» means a kind of spiritual power or angelic order.
fact: In 1337 Moscow was «a small principality» paying tribute to the Golden Horde.
exercise: «Moscow was a small principality, a land ruled by a prince.» What is a principality? | *A land ruled by a prince or princess | A type of church bell | A school for young princes | A large sea with many islands
exercise: Ella says «the Principality» means a princess's palace. Which meaning is right? | Another word for a church | *In the UK it is often a name for Wales | The name of a Golden Horde leader | A palace in Moscow
exercise: Find and copy the word for the yearly payment a ruled land makes to its overlord. «Ivan III stopped paying tribute, the yearly payment of a ruled land to its overlord.» | Horde | *tribute | overlord | Ivan
test: Which of these is a small principality in Europe? | Brazil | Egypt | *Monaco | Japan
test: What does «principalities» mean in «principalities and powers» from the Bible? | *Spiritual powers or angelic orders | A kind of church music | A group of countries at war | Princes who rule cities
exam: «In 1253 Prince Danylo received a royal crown from a papal envoy.» What is a papal envoy? | A prince of Halych | *A messenger of the Pope | A Mongol warrior | A palace guard
